# 39. Practical Troubleshooting

## Scenario 1: No IP Address

User says:

> "My computer is connected to the network, but I don't have Internet."

Run:

```cmd
ipconfig /all
```

Check whether the system has a valid IP address.

If it has an address such as:

```text
169.254.x.x
```

the system may have failed to obtain an IPv4 address from DHCP.

Investigate:

* DHCP server
* Network cable/Wi-Fi
* VLAN
* NIC
* DHCP configuration

---

## Scenario 2: IP Address Exists but Internet Doesn't Work

Check:

```text
IP address
Subnet mask
Default gateway
DNS server
```

Then test:

```cmd
ping <default-gateway>
```

If successful:

```cmd
ping 8.8.8.8
```

If that works, test:

```cmd
nslookup google.com
```

This helps isolate whether the issue is local connectivity, Internet routing, or DNS.

