# 40. Important IP Address Concepts

### Network Address

Identifies the subnet itself.

Example:

```text
192.168.1.0/24
```

### Broadcast Address

IPv4 address used to reach all hosts on a subnet.

Example:

```text
192.168.1.255
```

for `192.168.1.0/24`.

### Host Address

An address assigned to a device/interface.

Example:

```text
192.168.1.10
```

### Loopback

Used by a device to communicate with itself.

IPv4:

```text
127.0.0.1
```

IPv6:

```text
::1
```

